# --- Generated data ---
# data/ is 118 MB and fully reproducible: `python -m football.run_all` rebuilds
# it from matches_detailed_processed/ plus a download. models/ and reports/ are
# likewise outputs, not sources.
# Leading slash matters: a bare `data/` also matches football/data/, which is
# the merge/filter/audit package, and would silently drop it from the repo.
/data/
/models/
/reports/

# The scraped match CSVs under matches_detailed/ and matches_detailed_processed/
# ARE tracked, deliberately. They cannot be regenerated -- the goal.com scrapers
# stopped matching the site's markup -- so they are the one irreplaceable thing
# in this repository. The same goes for the derived CSVs in filter/, merged/ and
# performance/, kept because they are cheap relative to losing them.

